# One chip against the planet: which is bigger?
subtitle: "One computer chip against everyone on Earth, then against all the chickens eaten in a year: pick the bigger, and hear two hosts argue about it."
tags: ["computing","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"One chip vs the whole planet\" note \"2,300 in 1971\""

## One chip against the planet: which is bigger?
feedback:
    style: dry
    perfect: You think like a chip designer.
    good: Most people underrate the chip.
    poor: Nobody expects the chickens.
    none: The chickens win again.
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: 'Moore''s law: The number of transistors per microprocessor'
      authors: Our World in Data, from Karl Rupp (2022)
      year: 2022
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/transistors-per-microprocessor
      finding: about 2,300 transistors per microprocessor in 1971 and about 58.2 billion in 2021
    - id: pop
      title: Population
      authors: Our World in Data, from UN World Population Prospects
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/population
      finding: world population about 7.95 billion in 2021
    - id: chick
      title: Number of animals slaughtered for meat
      authors: Our World in Data, from FAO
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/animals-slaughtered-for-meat
      finding: about 78.5 billion chickens slaughtered for meat in 2024

