    card title "One chip vs the planet: which is bigger?"

A: How many tiny switches, called transistors, fit on one computer chip today?
    group chip members ["body","die","pl0","pr0","pl1","pr1","pl2","pr2","pl3","pr3","pl4","pr4","pl5","pr5","pt0","pb0","pt1","pb1","pt2","pb2","pt3","pb3","pt4","pb4"]

A: The first microprocessor, Intel's 4004 in 1971, had about two thousand three hundred.
    text t1971 "1971: 2,300" #3d3833 cites ["owid"] x 210 y 425 font_size 40

B: So today, what, a few million? It's still one little chip.
    highlight t1971

A: Let's settle it with a duel: one chip from 2021 against two rivals.
    cards duel cites ["owid","pop","chick"] size 1.5 x 400 y 590 width 600 unit billion compare "Which is bigger?" pairs [[0,1],[1,2]]
        * "People on Earth" icon.of "globe showing europe-africa" icon.set twemoji value 7.9
        * "One 2021 chip" icon.of "desktop computer" icon.set twemoji value 58.2
        * "Chickens eaten / year" icon.of chicken icon.set twemoji value 78.5

    ask "Tap the bigger number in each pair." on duel store d stage own
        right: One chip beats every person on Earth, and the chickens still beat the chip.
        wrong: {d} of {d.total}. The chip is bigger than you think, but not big enough for the chickens.

    erase duel t1971

B: Wait. One chip has more switches than there are people on the planet?
    text big "58 billion" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 210 y 425 font_size 52

A: Fifty-eight billion of them. That's about seven for every person alive, on one chip.
    text per "≈ 7 per person" #2f6b8f cites ["owid","pop"] x 680 y 470 font_size 60

A: From two thousand three hundred to fifty-eight billion: twenty-five million times more in fifty years.
    text times "×25 million since 1971" #8f887c x 680 y 360 font_size 44

B: Seven each, and I never got mine. I'd like them back, please.
    highlight per

